the proxy pattern, as the name implies,
allow us to create a proxy or an agent for a real object.

sometimes we need just a partial of an objects.
so instead load whole obj, we create an proxy at the middle
to just load what we need!
and we can do something at this middle layer
like logging, access control, caching,...

Imagine we are going to build an application for reading ebooks,
we have "Library" class that contain all user's book,

problem: when application load,
         all user's book get loaded (because we need to load library obj)
         but he just need one of them, so we bring some data to RAM, that
         we don't want it!

Note: we need library obj
      it's our domain
      but we should desig n it somehow, that show all the books
      but load base on demanded!